            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/recipes-fb/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Its not clear to me why we need a retry on a retry and how that is fixing the problem.\n\nIf `[ -f \"$NET_CONFIG_FILE\" ]` is true, and `! grep -q \"^DUIDType=\" \"$NET_CONFIG_FILE\"` is true, we add the LL settings and break. Else we say its already there and break. The added for loop will end up doing that 3 time unconditionally -- which I am not understanding how it is considered an extra check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/recipes-fb/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Hsu",
                        "email": "jason-hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "QuantaJasonHsu"
                    },
                    "message": "Please refer to this JIRA: https://metainfra.atlassian.net/browse/CLRMC-96\n.\nWe found that on certain FAB2 boards, during BMC boot, the Entity Manager has not yet written the MAC address to the Inventory when the Network service start. As a result, the Network service restart, and during that restart it overwrites 00-bmc-eth0.network with a version missing the DUID-LL settings.\n\nBecause this issue occurs intermittently, we need to extend and increase the retry duration. After our verification, running the check three times is sufficient to cover the time needed for all related services to complete their initialization. Therefore, we modified the script so that the added for loop runs three times unconditionally."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/recipes-fb/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Hsu",
                        "email": "jason-hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "QuantaJasonHsu"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @amithash@meta.com, could you help check this issue? Thank you"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/recipes-fb/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll/reconfig-interface-duid-ll",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Ideally this would get fixed in phosphor-networkd so that we can program the DUID type directly by phosphor-networkd."
                }
            ],
